      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:h6tcd37yr7vk33uuisbidqvw/bafkreiaa5eogk4fixv7tsdesale4iyhqunvlulie64vznv6rfuruy7ezqi",
      "alt": "A hand-drawn, xkcd-style line graph titled “Over time, I got better at telling the difference.” The y-axis is labeled “Probability” and runs from 0.0 to 1.0. The x-axis is labeled “Time” and runs from 1/1/2025 to “Today,” with ticks every two months (1/1/2025, 3/1/2025, 5/1/2025, 7/1/2025, 9/1/2025, 11/1/2025).\n\nTwo lines are plotted. A red line, labeled “Probability that Claude just said something ridiculous,” starts at about 0.92 in January 2025 and declines steadily to about 0.5 by November 2025. A blue line, labeled “Probability that I just misunderstood what Claude said,” starts at about 0.07 in January 2025 and rises steadily to about 0.5 by November 2025.\n\nThe two lines meet at 0.5 at a vertical dashed line marked “Opus 4.5 (Nov 2025).” After that point the trends speed up: the red line drops sharply to about 0.24 by “Today,” and the blue line climbs sharply to about 0.78. The joke is that the author’s growing skill at “telling the difference” mostly consists of realizing that, with newer Claude models, the confusing part is increasingly their own misunderstanding rather than Claude’s mistake.",
